NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have "},{"type":"link","href":"./code-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":" working on your server — the LLM writes and executes TypeScript, and you get results back. But your users see nothing while the sandbox runs. By the end of this guide, your React app will show real-time execution progress: console output, external function calls, and final results as they stream in."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-events-reach-the-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How events reach the client"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When code runs inside the sandbox, Code Mode emits "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"custom events"}]},{"type":"text","value":" through the AG-UI streaming protocol. These events travel alongside normal chat chunks (text, tool calls) and arrive in your client via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" callback."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The events emitted during each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":" call:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Event"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key fields"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:execution_started"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandbox begins executing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamp"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeLength"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:console"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console.log/error/warn/info"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"level"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"message"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamp"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:external_call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" function runs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"function"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamp"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:external_result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After a successful "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"function"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:external_error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" call fails"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"function"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every event includes a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","value":" that ties it to the specific "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":" tool call, so you can render events alongside the right message."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"listening-to-events-with-usechat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Listening to events with useChat"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" callback to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":". The callback receives the event type, payload, and a context object with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useCallback, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\ninterface VMEvent {\n  id: string;\n  eventType: string;\n  data: unknown;\n  timestamp: number;\n}\n\nexport function CodeModeChat() {\n  const [toolCallEvents, setToolCallEvents] = useState<\n    Map<string, Array<VMEvent>>\n  >(new Map());\n  const eventIdCounter = useRef(0);\n\n  const handleCustomEvent = useCallback(\n    (\n      eventType: string,\n      data: unknown,\n      context: { toolCallId?: string },\n    ) => {\n      const { toolCallId } = context;\n      if (!toolCallId) return;\n\n      const event: VMEvent = {\n        id: `event-${eventIdCounter.current++}`,\n        eventType,\n        data,\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      };\n\n      setToolCallEvents((prev) => {\n        const next = new Map(prev);\n        const events = next.get(toolCallId) || [];\n        next.set(toolCallId, [...events, event]);\n        return next;\n      });\n    },\n    [],\n  );\n\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    onCustomEvent: handleCustomEvent,\n  });\n\n  // Render messages with events — see next section\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=code-mode-client"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Events are keyed by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","value":" so each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":" call gets its own event timeline."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rendering-execution-progress","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering execution progress"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When rendering messages, check for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":" tool calls and display their events:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function MessageList({\n  messages,\n  toolCallEvents,\n}: {\n  messages: Array<{ id: string; role: string; parts: Array<any> }>;\n  toolCallEvents: Map<string, Array<VMEvent>>;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part) => {\n            if (part.type === \"text\") {\n              return <p key={part.id}>{part.content}</p>;\n            }\n\n            if (\n              part.type === \"tool-call\" &&\n              part.name === \"execute_typescript\"\n            ) {\n              const events = toolCallEvents.get(part.id) || [];\n              const result = part.output;\n\n              return (\n                <div key={part.id}>\n                  <CodeExecutionPanel\n                    code={part.input?.typescriptCode}\n                    events={events}\n                    result={result}\n                    isRunning={!result}\n                  />\n                </div>\n              );\n            }\n\n            return null;\n          })}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=code-mode-client"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"building-an-execution-panel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Building an execution panel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here's a complete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeExecutionPanel"},{"type":"text","value":" component that shows the generated code, live event stream, and final result:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function CodeExecutionPanel({\n  code,\n  events,\n  result,\n  isRunning,\n}: {\n  code?: string;\n  events: Array<VMEvent>;\n  result?: { success: boolean; result?: unknown; logs?: string[]; error?: { message: string } };\n  isRunning: boolean;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"border rounded-lg overflow-hidden my-2\">\n      {/* Generated code */}\n      {code && (\n        <details open>\n          <summary className=\"px-3 py-2 bg-gray-100 font-mono text-sm cursor-pointer\">\n            TypeScript code\n          </summary>\n          <pre className=\"p-3 text-sm overflow-x-auto bg-gray-50\">\n            <code>{code}</code>\n          </pre>\n        </details>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Live event stream */}\n      {events.length > 0 && (\n        <div className=\"border-t px-3 py-2\">\n          <div className=\"text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500 mb-1\">\n            Execution log\n          </div>\n          <div className=\"space-y-1 font-mono text-xs\">\n            {events.map((event) => (\n              <EventLine key={event.id} event={event} />\n            ))}\n            {isRunning && (\n              <div className=\"text-blue-500 animate-pulse\">Running...</div>\n            )}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Final result */}\n      {result && (\n        <div\n          className={`border-t px-3 py-2 text-sm ${\n            result.success ? \"bg-green-50\" : \"bg-red-50\"\n          }`}\n        >\n          {result.error && (\n            <div className=\"text-red-700\">Error: {result.error.message}</div>\n          )}\n          {result.logs && result.logs.length > 0 && (\n            <pre className=\"text-gray-600 text-xs mt-1\">\n              {result.logs.join(\"\\n\")}\n            </pre>\n          )}\n          {result.success && result.result !== undefined && (\n            <pre className=\"text-green-800 text-xs mt-1\">\n              {JSON.stringify(result.result, null, 2)}\n            </pre>\n          )}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction isRecord(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {\n  return typeof value === \"object\" && value !== null;\n}\n\nfunction EventLine({ event }: { event: VMEvent }) {\n  if (!isRecord(event.data)) return null;\n  const data = event.data;\n\n  switch (event.eventType) {\n    case \"code_mode:console\":\n      return (\n        <div\n          className={\n            data.level === \"error\"\n              ? \"text-red-600\"\n              : data.level === \"warn\"\n                ? \"text-yellow-600\"\n                : \"text-gray-600\"\n          }\n        >\n          [{String(data.level)}] {String(data.message)}\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:external_call\":\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-amber-600\">\n          → {String(data.function)}(\n          {JSON.stringify(data.args)})\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:external_result\":\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-green-600\">\n          ← {String(data.function)} ({String(data.duration)}ms)\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:external_error\":\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-red-600\">\n          ✗ {String(data.function)}: {String(data.error)}\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:execution_started\":\n      return <div className=\"text-cyan-600\">▶ Execution started</div>;\n\n    default:\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-gray-400\">\n          {event.eventType}: {JSON.stringify(data)}\n        </div>\n      );\n  }\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=code-mode-client"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This gives you:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A collapsible code block showing the TypeScript the model wrote"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A live event log showing console output, external function calls with arguments, results with durations, and errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A status-colored result panel with logs and the return value"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"adapting-for-other-frameworks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapting for other frameworks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" callback is available through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClient"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client"},{"type":"text","value":", which all framework integrations use under the hood. In Solid, Vue, or Svelte, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" in the same way you pass it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" in React — the callback signature is identical:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"(eventType: string, data: unknown, context: { toolCallId?: string }) => void","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./code-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for setting up the server side, and "},{"type":"link","href":"./code-mode-with-snippets","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode with Snippets"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for adding persistent snippet libraries."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"how-events-reach-the-client","text":"How events reach the client","level":2},{"id":"listening-to-events-with-usechat","text":"Listening to events with useChat","level":2},{"id":"rendering-execution-progress","text":"Rendering execution progress","level":2},{"id":"building-an-execution-panel","text":"Building an execution panel","level":2},{"id":"adapting-for-other-frameworks","text":"Adapting for other frameworks","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have [Code Mode](./code-mode) working on your server — the LLM writes and executes TypeScript, and you get results back. But your users see nothing while the sandbox runs. By the end of this guide, your React app will show real-time execution progress: console output, external function calls, and final results as they stream in.\n\n## How events reach the client\n\nWhen code runs inside the sandbox, Code Mode emits **custom events** through the AG-UI streaming protocol. These events travel alongside normal chat chunks (text, tool calls) and arrive in your client via the `onCustomEvent` callback.\n\nThe events emitted during each `execute_typescript` call:\n\n| Event | When | Key fields |\n|-------|------|------------|\n| `code_mode:execution_started` | Sandbox begins executing | `timestamp`, `codeLength` |\n| `code_mode:console` | Each `console.log/error/warn/info` | `level`, `message`, `timestamp` |\n| `code_mode:external_call` | Before an `external_*` function runs | `function`, `args`, `timestamp` |\n| `code_mode:external_result` | After a successful `external_*` call | `function`, `result`, `duration` |\n| `code_mode:external_error` | When an `external_*` call fails | `function`, `error`, `duration` |\n\nEvery event includes a `toolCallId` that ties it to the specific `execute_typescript` tool call, so you can render events alongside the right message.\n\n## Listening to events with useChat\n\nPass an `onCustomEvent` callback to `useChat`. The callback receives the event type, payload, and a context object with the `toolCallId`:\n\n```tsx group=code-mode-client\nimport { useCallback, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\ninterface VMEvent {\n  id: string;\n  eventType: string;\n  data: unknown;\n  timestamp: number;\n}\n\nexport function CodeModeChat() {\n  const [toolCallEvents, setToolCallEvents] = useState<\n    Map<string, Array<VMEvent>>\n  >(new Map());\n  const eventIdCounter = useRef(0);\n\n  const handleCustomEvent = useCallback(\n    (\n      eventType: string,\n      data: unknown,\n      context: { toolCallId?: string },\n    ) => {\n      const { toolCallId } = context;\n      if (!toolCallId) return;\n\n      const event: VMEvent = {\n        id: `event-${eventIdCounter.current++}`,\n        eventType,\n        data,\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      };\n\n      setToolCallEvents((prev) => {\n        const next = new Map(prev);\n        const events = next.get(toolCallId) || [];\n        next.set(toolCallId, [...events, event]);\n        return next;\n      });\n    },\n    [],\n  );\n\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    onCustomEvent: handleCustomEvent,\n  });\n\n  // Render messages with events — see next section\n}\n```\n\nEvents are keyed by `toolCallId` so each `execute_typescript` call gets its own event timeline.\n\n## Rendering execution progress\n\nWhen rendering messages, check for `execute_typescript` tool calls and display their events:\n\n```tsx group=code-mode-client\nfunction MessageList({\n  messages,\n  toolCallEvents,\n}: {\n  messages: Array<{ id: string; role: string; parts: Array<any> }>;\n  toolCallEvents: Map<string, Array<VMEvent>>;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part) => {\n            if (part.type === \"text\") {\n              return <p key={part.id}>{part.content}</p>;\n            }\n\n            if (\n              part.type === \"tool-call\" &&\n              part.name === \"execute_typescript\"\n            ) {\n              const events = toolCallEvents.get(part.id) || [];\n              const result = part.output;\n\n              return (\n                <div key={part.id}>\n                  <CodeExecutionPanel\n                    code={part.input?.typescriptCode}\n                    events={events}\n                    result={result}\n                    isRunning={!result}\n                  />\n                </div>\n              );\n            }\n\n            return null;\n          })}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Building an execution panel\n\nHere's a complete `CodeExecutionPanel` component that shows the generated code, live event stream, and final result:\n\n```tsx group=code-mode-client\nfunction CodeExecutionPanel({\n  code,\n  events,\n  result,\n  isRunning,\n}: {\n  code?: string;\n  events: Array<VMEvent>;\n  result?: { success: boolean; result?: unknown; logs?: string[]; error?: { message: string } };\n  isRunning: boolean;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"border rounded-lg overflow-hidden my-2\">\n      {/* Generated code */}\n      {code && (\n        <details open>\n          <summary className=\"px-3 py-2 bg-gray-100 font-mono text-sm cursor-pointer\">\n            TypeScript code\n          </summary>\n          <pre className=\"p-3 text-sm overflow-x-auto bg-gray-50\">\n            <code>{code}</code>\n          </pre>\n        </details>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Live event stream */}\n      {events.length > 0 && (\n        <div className=\"border-t px-3 py-2\">\n          <div className=\"text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500 mb-1\">\n            Execution log\n          </div>\n          <div className=\"space-y-1 font-mono text-xs\">\n            {events.map((event) => (\n              <EventLine key={event.id} event={event} />\n            ))}\n            {isRunning && (\n              <div className=\"text-blue-500 animate-pulse\">Running...</div>\n            )}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Final result */}\n      {result && (\n        <div\n          className={`border-t px-3 py-2 text-sm ${\n            result.success ? \"bg-green-50\" : \"bg-red-50\"\n          }`}\n        >\n          {result.error && (\n            <div className=\"text-red-700\">Error: {result.error.message}</div>\n          )}\n          {result.logs && result.logs.length > 0 && (\n            <pre className=\"text-gray-600 text-xs mt-1\">\n              {result.logs.join(\"\\n\")}\n            </pre>\n          )}\n          {result.success && result.result !== undefined && (\n            <pre className=\"text-green-800 text-xs mt-1\">\n              {JSON.stringify(result.result, null, 2)}\n            </pre>\n          )}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction isRecord(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {\n  return typeof value === \"object\" && value !== null;\n}\n\nfunction EventLine({ event }: { event: VMEvent }) {\n  if (!isRecord(event.data)) return null;\n  const data = event.data;\n\n  switch (event.eventType) {\n    case \"code_mode:console\":\n      return (\n        <div\n          className={\n            data.level === \"error\"\n              ? \"text-red-600\"\n              : data.level === \"warn\"\n                ? \"text-yellow-600\"\n                : \"text-gray-600\"\n          }\n        >\n          [{String(data.level)}] {String(data.message)}\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:external_call\":\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-amber-600\">\n          → {String(data.function)}(\n          {JSON.stringify(data.args)})\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:external_result\":\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-green-600\">\n          ← {String(data.function)} ({String(data.duration)}ms)\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:external_error\":\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-red-600\">\n          ✗ {String(data.function)}: {String(data.error)}\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:execution_started\":\n      return <div className=\"text-cyan-600\">▶ Execution started</div>;\n\n    default:\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-gray-400\">\n          {event.eventType}: {JSON.stringify(data)}\n        </div>\n      );\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis gives you:\n- A collapsible code block showing the TypeScript the model wrote\n- A live event log showing console output, external function calls with arguments, results with durations, and errors\n- A status-colored result panel with logs and the return value\n\n## Adapting for other frameworks\n\nThe `onCustomEvent` callback is available through `ChatClient` from `@tanstack/ai-client`, which all framework integrations use under the hood. In Solid, Vue, or Svelte, pass `onCustomEvent` in the same way you pass it to `useChat` in React — the callback signature is identical:\n\n```typescript ignore\n(eventType: string, data: unknown, context: { toolCallId?: string }) => void\n```\n\nSee [Code Mode](./code-mode) for setting up the server side, and [Code Mode with Snippets](./code-mode-with-snippets) for adding persistent snippet libraries.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Showing Code Mode in the UI\nid: code-mode-client-integration\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Stream Code Mode execution events to your React app — console output, external calls, and results as they happen, via onCustomEvent.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - code mode\n  - react ui\n  - custom events\n  - onCustomEvent\n  - streaming ui\n  - execution progress\n---\n\nYou have [Code Mode](./code-mode) working on your server — the LLM writes and executes TypeScript, and you get results back. But your users see nothing while the sandbox runs. By the end of this guide, your React app will show real-time execution progress: console output, external function calls, and final results as they stream in.\n\n## How events reach the client\n\nWhen code runs inside the sandbox, Code Mode emits **custom events** through the AG-UI streaming protocol. These events travel alongside normal chat chunks (text, tool calls) and arrive in your client via the `onCustomEvent` callback.\n\nThe events emitted during each `execute_typescript` call:\n\n| Event | When | Key fields |\n|-------|------|------------|\n| `code_mode:execution_started` | Sandbox begins executing | `timestamp`, `codeLength` |\n| `code_mode:console` | Each `console.log/error/warn/info` | `level`, `message`, `timestamp` |\n| `code_mode:external_call` | Before an `external_*` function runs | `function`, `args`, `timestamp` |\n| `code_mode:external_result` | After a successful `external_*` call | `function`, `result`, `duration` |\n| `code_mode:external_error` | When an `external_*` call fails | `function`, `error`, `duration` |\n\nEvery event includes a `toolCallId` that ties it to the specific `execute_typescript` tool call, so you can render events alongside the right message.\n\n## Listening to events with useChat\n\nPass an `onCustomEvent` callback to `useChat`. The callback receives the event type, payload, and a context object with the `toolCallId`:\n\n```tsx group=code-mode-client\nimport { useCallback, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\ninterface VMEvent {\n  id: string;\n  eventType: string;\n  data: unknown;\n  timestamp: number;\n}\n\nexport function CodeModeChat() {\n  const [toolCallEvents, setToolCallEvents] = useState<\n    Map<string, Array<VMEvent>>\n  >(new Map());\n  const eventIdCounter = useRef(0);\n\n  const handleCustomEvent = useCallback(\n    (\n      eventType: string,\n      data: unknown,\n      context: { toolCallId?: string },\n    ) => {\n      const { toolCallId } = context;\n      if (!toolCallId) return;\n\n      const event: VMEvent = {\n        id: `event-${eventIdCounter.current++}`,\n        eventType,\n        data,\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n      };\n\n      setToolCallEvents((prev) => {\n        const next = new Map(prev);\n        const events = next.get(toolCallId) || [];\n        next.set(toolCallId, [...events, event]);\n        return next;\n      });\n    },\n    [],\n  );\n\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    onCustomEvent: handleCustomEvent,\n  });\n\n  // Render messages with events — see next section\n}\n```\n\nEvents are keyed by `toolCallId` so each `execute_typescript` call gets its own event timeline.\n\n## Rendering execution progress\n\nWhen rendering messages, check for `execute_typescript` tool calls and display their events:\n\n```tsx group=code-mode-client\nfunction MessageList({\n  messages,\n  toolCallEvents,\n}: {\n  messages: Array<{ id: string; role: string; parts: Array<any> }>;\n  toolCallEvents: Map<string, Array<VMEvent>>;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part) => {\n            if (part.type === \"text\") {\n              return <p key={part.id}>{part.content}</p>;\n            }\n\n            if (\n              part.type === \"tool-call\" &&\n              part.name === \"execute_typescript\"\n            ) {\n              const events = toolCallEvents.get(part.id) || [];\n              const result = part.output;\n\n              return (\n                <div key={part.id}>\n                  <CodeExecutionPanel\n                    code={part.input?.typescriptCode}\n                    events={events}\n                    result={result}\n                    isRunning={!result}\n                  />\n                </div>\n              );\n            }\n\n            return null;\n          })}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Building an execution panel\n\nHere's a complete `CodeExecutionPanel` component that shows the generated code, live event stream, and final result:\n\n```tsx group=code-mode-client\nfunction CodeExecutionPanel({\n  code,\n  events,\n  result,\n  isRunning,\n}: {\n  code?: string;\n  events: Array<VMEvent>;\n  result?: { success: boolean; result?: unknown; logs?: string[]; error?: { message: string } };\n  isRunning: boolean;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"border rounded-lg overflow-hidden my-2\">\n      {/* Generated code */}\n      {code && (\n        <details open>\n          <summary className=\"px-3 py-2 bg-gray-100 font-mono text-sm cursor-pointer\">\n            TypeScript code\n          </summary>\n          <pre className=\"p-3 text-sm overflow-x-auto bg-gray-50\">\n            <code>{code}</code>\n          </pre>\n        </details>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Live event stream */}\n      {events.length > 0 && (\n        <div className=\"border-t px-3 py-2\">\n          <div className=\"text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500 mb-1\">\n            Execution log\n          </div>\n          <div className=\"space-y-1 font-mono text-xs\">\n            {events.map((event) => (\n              <EventLine key={event.id} event={event} />\n            ))}\n            {isRunning && (\n              <div className=\"text-blue-500 animate-pulse\">Running...</div>\n            )}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Final result */}\n      {result && (\n        <div\n          className={`border-t px-3 py-2 text-sm ${\n            result.success ? \"bg-green-50\" : \"bg-red-50\"\n          }`}\n        >\n          {result.error && (\n            <div className=\"text-red-700\">Error: {result.error.message}</div>\n          )}\n          {result.logs && result.logs.length > 0 && (\n            <pre className=\"text-gray-600 text-xs mt-1\">\n              {result.logs.join(\"\\n\")}\n            </pre>\n          )}\n          {result.success && result.result !== undefined && (\n            <pre className=\"text-green-800 text-xs mt-1\">\n              {JSON.stringify(result.result, null, 2)}\n            </pre>\n          )}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction isRecord(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {\n  return typeof value === \"object\" && value !== null;\n}\n\nfunction EventLine({ event }: { event: VMEvent }) {\n  if (!isRecord(event.data)) return null;\n  const data = event.data;\n\n  switch (event.eventType) {\n    case \"code_mode:console\":\n      return (\n        <div\n          className={\n            data.level === \"error\"\n              ? \"text-red-600\"\n              : data.level === \"warn\"\n                ? \"text-yellow-600\"\n                : \"text-gray-600\"\n          }\n        >\n          [{String(data.level)}] {String(data.message)}\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:external_call\":\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-amber-600\">\n          → {String(data.function)}(\n          {JSON.stringify(data.args)})\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:external_result\":\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-green-600\">\n          ← {String(data.function)} ({String(data.duration)}ms)\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:external_error\":\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-red-600\">\n          ✗ {String(data.function)}: {String(data.error)}\n        </div>\n      );\n\n    case \"code_mode:execution_started\":\n      return <div className=\"text-cyan-600\">▶ Execution started</div>;\n\n    default:\n      return (\n        <div className=\"text-gray-400\">\n          {event.eventType}: {JSON.stringify(data)}\n        </div>\n      );\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis gives you:\n- A collapsible code block showing the TypeScript the model wrote\n- A live event log showing console output, external function calls with arguments, results with durations, and errors\n- A status-colored result panel with logs and the return value\n\n## Adapting for other frameworks\n\nThe `onCustomEvent` callback is available through `ChatClient` from `@tanstack/ai-client`, which all framework integrations use under the hood. In Solid, Vue, or Svelte, pass `onCustomEvent` in the same way you pass it to `useChat` in React — the callback signature is identical:\n\n```typescript ignore\n(eventType: string, data: unknown, context: { toolCallId?: string }) => void\n```\n\nSee [Code Mode](./code-mode) for setting up the server side, and [Code Mode with Snippets](./code-mode-with-snippets) for adding persistent snippet libraries.\n"}
